{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the fixed-slot fixtures for request 121a8913 (uniqueness guards by index), answering 1b4592ac.\n\n1. The scan-specific corpus may declare the name slot non-fixed. In packages/derive/test/definition-corpus/forms-guards-data.ts, change job.name to `fixed: false` and keep every row, body, deadline and expectation of forms-guards-variants.ts and forms-guards.test.ts as they are. That corpus exists to prove the three results of the list forms under a stopped scan (section 6.5); it is not a witness of the index rule, and a fixture that happens to declare `fixed: true` does not make it one. The request's clause \"the existing guard tests unchanged\" means their assertions, which this keeps. The note records the one-line corpus change and why.\n\n2. The index rule gets its own witnesses, new in the derive tests: a type with a fixed slot, a range guard whose `where` is exactly one `equals` between that slot and a constant, and the same against a field, each under guardScan 3 with more items than the bound; both answer complete counts (guard-failed or passes, never guard-incomplete). Paired control in the same file: the same guard on a non-fixed slot of the same type still answers guard-incomplete past the bound. Do not resolve the conflict by omitting constants or by special-casing small guardScan values.\n\n3. Operands. The decided rule covers a `field` or a `const` operand. An `element` operand of a list is outside the fast path unless it falls out of the same code with no extra branch; the merge act of the shared corpus therefore keeps its scan either way, and nothing in this ruling changes it.\n\n4. Room replay means `dap verify --all` against the room. The request's \"`dap check` replays it\" was written before DX-A1 sent `dap check` to local application-package validation. The witness is: `dap verify --all` on the 2,000-member room reports every scope consistent after the index is part of the derived view it rebuilds. A `dap check` scenario of the rule is welcome if it is cheap, and is not required.\n\nEverything else in 121a8913 stands: one gate, exact-head review, the PD-2 note with its manifest under 4e199bd8. c3034274 continues in its gate first.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}